# MadGraph5 batch script: e+ e- > mu+ mu- at LO (default coupling orders).
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - The smallest complete amplitude in the set: two massless colourless
#     fermion lines joined by an s-channel gamma*/Z, one diagram, one colour
#     flow. Nothing is entangled with anything else, so when a convention change
#     moves a number this is the row that says whether the change was in the
#     spinors, the propagator or the couplings.
#   - It is the reference point every other row is measured against: the
#     |M|^2 grid, the analytic QED cross section and the VEGAS sigma all meet
#     here, which is why it is also the process the kernel-composition and
#     Fortran77-HELAS gates use.
#   - Beams at 45.6 + 45.6 GeV put sqrt(s) on the Z pole, where the gamma*/Z
#     interference is largest and a wrong relative sign between the two
#     mediators cannot hide inside the photon term.
#
# Default orders at tree level are QED=2; there is no QCD contribution to
# constrain, so this script has no explicit-order counterpart.
#
# lpp defaults to 0 for lepton beams: fixed-energy partonic kinematics.
generate e+ e- > mu+ mu-
output ee_to_mumu -nojpeg
launch
  set ebeam1 45.6
  set ebeam2 45.6
  done
